/*! \page Verification_intro Verification and diagnostics

\section Verification_intro_introduction Introduction

Every run reports two conservation residuals. They are computed by the function \ref py_utils::post_process::calculate_derived_quantities "calculate_derived_quantities()" in radcluster_code/py_utils/post_process.py.

\section Verification_intro_fp Frenkel-pair residual

Let \f$S_I(t) = \sum_n n\,c_n\f$ be the SIA inventory and \f$S(t) = \sum_m m\,c_m\f$ the swelling. The swelling is reported through the identity

\f[
S(t) = S_I(t) + \Delta J^d(t) ,
\f]

where \f$\Delta J^d\f$ is the cumulative net bias flux to dislocations. The identity yields the dimensionless Frenkel-pair residual

\f[
\delta_{FP}(t) = \frac{\left| S(t) - S_I(t) - \Delta J^d(t) \right|}{S(t) + S_I(t) + \Delta J^d(t)} .
\f]

\section Verification_intro_he Helium residual

The helium balance yields the residual \f$\delta_{He}(t)\f$, which compares the helium in solution and in cavities with the helium that was produced and lost at sinks.

\section Verification_intro_levels Levels

Both residuals should stay below about \f$10^{-6}\f$. A value above \f$10^{-3}\f$ indicates a coding error.

\b Note that in long loop-coarsening runs the loop distribution can outgrow the size axis. Products beyond the largest tracked size then carry content out of the domain, and \f$\delta_{FP}\f$ grows. It falls as the largest tracked size grows.

\section Verification_intro_scripts Check scripts

The folder radcluster_code/codes/Python_Testing holds standalone scripts that gate the physics:
- helium and Frenkel-pair conservation
- bin-moment against discrete equivalence
- convergence in the size of the discrete prefix
- loop-conversion kernels and conservation
- consistency of the graph declaration
- comparisons of linear solvers and of window modes
- benchmarks of the Woodbury preconditioner
- parameter sweeps

A change that touches reaction kernels or stoichiometry should come with the relevant conservation check, and with a note of the resulting \f$\delta_{FP}\f$ and \f$\delta_{He}\f$.

\section Verification_intro_pages Pages

- \subpage Verification_digitalTwin

\sa \ref IO_output, \ref Core_graphWalker

*/
